1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,527
CHAPTER 4 — THE GREATEST MOVIE NEVER MADE

2
00:00:04,827 --> 00:00:13,355
In the mid-seventies, Chilean director Alejandro Jodorowsky wanted to bring Dune to the big screen. And he wanted to do it on a massive scale.

3
00:00:13,535 --> 00:00:18,667
Comic artist Moebius drew some 3,000 storyboards to plan every single shot.

4
00:00:18,847 --> 00:00:28,508
He recruited Swiss artist H. R. Giger, Pink Floyd for the music, and Salvador Dalí as the Emperor. Dalí asked for $100,000 an hour.

5
00:00:28,688 --> 00:00:34,726
The script would have run for more than ten hours. No Hollywood studio was willing to pay for it.

6
00:00:34,906 --> 00:00:38,830
They spent $2 million, and the project collapsed.

7
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:44,939
But part of that team stayed together. A few years later, they reunited to make Alien.
